t.dc.html","UpdateRequired.dc.html","UpdateRequiredLight.dc.html","Logos.dc.html","BuckVariants.dc.html"],"notes":{"exam-prep-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Flow 1 — Working on it: from first launch to passing the real exam","kind":"title1","maxW":8380,"page":"exam-prep"},"exam-prep-light":{"x":0,"y":1040,"text":"Light mode","kind":"title1","maxW":8380,"page":"exam-prep"},"exam-prep-steps":{"x":0,"y":880,"w":2270,"text":"Steps: 1 splash → 2 “Working on it” → 3 what you hunt with (firearm, bow, crossbow) → 4 where you hunt (Québec, Alberta, elsewhere in Canada): the province sets the quizzes — Québec: Québec hunter course; Alberta: Alberta course + PAL; elsewhere: PAL → 5 Home → 6 Exam training → 7–8 practice and results (8b nothing to review) → 9 Mock exams: ten per exam, each with its best and last score → 10–11 a mock and its results (10b quit; the first try of a mock ends with the interstitial; results offer “Next mock” or “All mocks”) → 12 retaking a finished mock, or 14 “Reset all” once all ten are done, needs a rewarded ad watched to the end, and that run shows no interstitial; 13 offline: no ad, no retake → 15 “I passed the real exam” → 16 Home as a Hunter (the same home as flow 2, with a congratulations banner and Exam training kept as a row).","color":"orange","size":"m","page":"exam-prep"},"what-is-it-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Flow 3 — What is it? (game identification)","kind":"title1","maxW":1800,"page":"what-is-it"},"what-is-it-light":{"x":0,"y":1040,"text":"Light mode","kind":"title1","maxW":1800,"page":"what-is-it"},"what-is-it-steps":{"x":0,"y":880,"w":1800,"text":"From Home's “What is it?” tile: the hub → a photo question (tap the photo for full screen) → the answer card.","color":"orange","size":"m","page":"what-is-it"},"settings-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Flow 4 — Settings and About","kind":"title1","maxW":3300,"page":"settings"},"settings-light":{"x":0,"y":1040,"text":"Light mode","kind":"title1","maxW":3300,"page":"settings"},"settings-steps":{"x":0,"y":880,"w":3210,"text":"Home's gear → Settings (hunter type, hunting with, where you hunt, language, daily goal) → My provinces (switch on another province to add its quizzes, or off to hide them) → About. Settings → Remove ads: 7 days for CA$1.99 (kept on this phone only, said under the offer and again before Play’s sheet) or forever for CA$14.99 (restored by Play); also linked from the mock exam retake dialog.","color":"orange","size":"m","page":"settings"},"system-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Flow 5 — System screens","kind":"title1","maxW":1800,"page":"system"},"system-light":{"x":0,"y":1040,"text":"Light mode","kind":"title1","maxW":1800,"page":"system"},"system-steps":{"x":0,"y":880,"w":860,"text":"Shown instead of the app when this version is below the force-update minimum (Remote Config).","color":"orange","size":"m","page":"system"},"logo-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Logo — the buck, and variants to make it ours","kind":"title1","maxW":2640,"page":"logo"},"hunter-title":{"x":0,"y":-260,"text":"Flow 2 — Hunter: licensed hunters, from first launch to the season","kind":"title1","maxW":11200,"page":"hunter"},"hunter-light":{"x":0,"y":1040,"text":"Light mode","kind":"title1","maxW":11200,"page":"hunter"},"hunter-steps":{"x":0,"y":880,"w":4150,"color":"orange","size":"m","page":"hunter","text":"Steps: 1 “Hunter” (licensed, whether it's the first season or the thirtieth) → 2 what you hunt with → 3 where you hunt: the province sets the rules and game → 4 first Home: an optional, dismissible “Already hunt? Skip what you know” card above today's questions → 5 a 15-question skill check across the field skills → 6 results: skills you ace start as mastered, the rest become practice → 7 Home, to stay up to date: today’s 6 questions, 3 species (photos, including look-alikes such as white-tailed or mule deer, sex and age; 7b) and 3 general (rules, safety, shot placement, tracking; 7c), then the What is it? and Field skills tiles; no exam → 8 done for today → 9 permission."},"hunter-skills":{"x":4230,"y":880,"w":2740,"color":"orange","size":"m","page":"hunter","text":"Field skills: 10 today’s mix (10 questions from the weakest skills) and readiness per skill — shot placement, after the shot, safe handling, rules in the field, survival → 11 skill question → 12 results, with the skill’s progress. Mastery: 13 a skill at 100% is mastered → 14 later, mastered skills show a check, and a skill whose right answers are over 3 months old fades back below 100%; each mix keeps 1–2 questions from mastered skills → 15 every skill mastered: the mix becomes “Keep your edge”."},"hunter-season":{"x":7050,"y":880,"w":4150,"color":"orange","size":"m","page":"hunter","text":"Season: the app doesn’t know legal season dates (zone, weapon, year). 16 without a date, from late August Home says “Hunting season is coming” and offers to set your date → 16b you pick your first hunting day (check the official regulations) → 16c remind me before my season? → 17 Home counts down to your date, 3 weeks before it → 18 the season check (15 questions, all skills). Reminders are local notifications, never asked at onboarding (8 or 16c, then 9), at most one a day, never between 9 pm and 8 am. 19 Settings: switches for both, and the season start date. 20 how they look on the lock screen."}},"designSystems":[]}